#! ia 1.0

@law approval-seal-target-branch-authority
  meaning
    says "The seal check reads who may sign (@approver) and which rules apply (@approval-rule), as well as which pattern records exist for @docket matched claims, exclusively from the target branch, never from unratified edits on the pull request head. A pull request cannot grant itself authority by adding an approver, loosening a rule or planting a pattern in the same change."
    answers "Which branch decides the approver roster, active rules and trusted patterns during a seal check?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Evaluate approver keys, approval rules and matched docket patterns solely from the target branch's ratified corpus, never from unratified head changes."
  subject
    subject-word approval
    subject-kind definition

@law approval-seal-exact-statement
  meaning
    says "An @approval seal is verified by rebuilding the SealStatement (purpose inventarch-approval, version 1) from the record's fields, serializing it with RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS), and verifying a canonical 64-byte Ed25519 signature (scalar S strictly below group order L) under a 32-byte public key whose SHA-256 base64url digest equals seal.key-id. seal.record-digest is the full compiled graph per-record digest, never a prose-only summary digest; any change to the record, its one-hop depends-on digests, its answered rule digests or (under current-revision rules) the corpus revision invalidates or stales the seal. Neither the kit nor the check ever holds a private key or contacts a network service."
    answers "What cryptographic statement must an @approval verify against, and what invalidates it?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Rebuild SealStatement from fields, canonicalize with RFC 8785 JCS, verify strict Ed25519 (S < L) against a target-branch public key matching seal.key-id, bind the full compiled record digest and one-hop dependencies, and run completely offline without private keys."
  subject
    subject-word approval
    subject-kind definition

@law approval-roster-and-rules-person-merge
  meaning
    says "Changes to @approver, @approval-rule and already-ratified @docket records are root authority changes: they obey the built-in roster floor regardless of looser rules, cannot merge automatically (demand.merge automatic is refused on root rules), cannot delete the last approver, and require target-branch first-parent history commitments for key revocations and delayed recovery or Slack route notices."
    answers "How are changes to approvers, approval rules and ratified dockets protected?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Enforce the built-in roster floor and person-only merge on every @approver, @approval-rule and target-branch @docket change, and refuse automatic merge or deletion of the sole approver."
  subject
    subject-word approval-rule
    subject-kind governance
